elden ring is a difficult game not only  in challenging combat but also in  cryptic and unclear instructions and  explanations and despite it being more  straightforward than his predecessors it  can still leave many things unclear the  difficulty of the gameplay the unsurety  of how certain mechanics work and the  high chance that a player might not even  notice they are missing some vital  aspect or mechanic can make things more  frustrating than they need be so this is  a short guide on how to get a good grasp  of the early game of eldon rank this  won't be an exhaustive list of  everything you can or should do but it  will be a straightforward guide about  how to get a based weapon learn some  mechanics and find some core items that  will put you in a good place to explore  the lands between without wanting to die  at least not as much  so the first fight is expected death and  the tutorial is straightforward so we're  ignoring them once we get into the world  step one is going to be getting our  weapon a curved greatsword called the  bloodhound fang it requires some  strength and dexterity stats to properly  wield so choose a starting class like  the samurai or warrior first location is  the church of ella which is about as  obvious as can be head there light the  bonfire and say hi to the smithing table  where you'll upgrade your weapon and  kill the merchant and don't leave the  church without touching the grace to  activate it races are your checkpoints  and fast travel locations so you always  want to activate them all the swirling  light around them makes them hard to  miss so be on the lookout for that as  you explore the world next we want our  steed torrent because foot travel is  slow you receive torrent after resting  at the gate front grace which is up the  road and to the left on the map head  there feel free to kill the mobs on the  way if you want souls you can sneak  attack them by crouching up to their  backs but they're not too hard either  way activate and rest at the grace and  melina will visit melina is the one who  lets you level up at grace sites she'll  give you a whistle to call torrent pop  that in your pouch and you're ready to  ride  now we'll be following the road east on  the way through the ruins pick up the  map on the pillar these unlock more  detail on your map screen and they show  up on the basic brown maps as small  pillars they're usually on or next to  main roads but they can be surprisingly  easy to miss especially if you're  wandering around on the sides there's  another grace on the other side of the  ruins and then we can head off when the  road forks go left and you'll soon find  a grace to the right  [Music]  activate and head southeast into the  forest there will be another pillar on  your map and you can find the east limb  grave map item  [Music]  there's also a minor urge tree nearby  which is basically just a really big  tree so it should be easy to find and  you can pick up some nice loot from that  too southwest from the tree and south  south east from the grace you'll find  mistwood ruins which has a big bear and  a big wolf you can hear the wolf howl on  the north side of the ruins  [Music]  once you hear the howling open up the  map and fast travel back to the church  of ella the place with the merchant and  the smithing table if it's nighttime you  might meet the witch rena she'll give  you items for summoning spirit ashes but  if she doesn't show up don't fret you  can buy the same items from another  merchant speak to kalei and ask him  about the halloween he'll tell you about  it and give you the snap gesture with  that head back to the ruins and snap why  the berserk reference will jump down and  you can speak to him again on the north  side of the ruins he's hunting for a man  named derewill that's who we're going to  get our weapon from the name's blythe  he fled somewhere nearby after speaking  to wolfman get back on the road and head  south  just below the fork will be a somber  smithing stone which we'll use to  upgrade our weapon  keep heading south until you find the  agil lake south brace just south of that  is an ever jail a zone that holds a boss  fight in it you'll find these fights  scattered throughout the game enter the  ever jail and summon bly you don't have  to but if you're trying to fight a boss  solo without leveling up this guide is  probably wasted on you the fight  shouldn't be too hard with blythe if you  let him take the aggro just watch out  for the quick dash attacks  emerge from the everglade victorious  with your new sword and you'll find  blythe present to give you a reward  another somber smithing stone chances  are you won't have stats to wield the  bloodhound fang immediately so put some  of the runes you got into dexterity if  you two hand the sword you won't need to  have the full strength requirement level  2 strength works just fine now we'll  head back once more to the church of  ella we want to upgrade the sword at the  smithing table but you might not have  enough rooms the ruins are a decent farm  and there's a valuable item down the set  of stairs or if you continue up the road  to the west you'll find good enemies to  farm too along the road you'll find a  golden seed to upgrade your healing  flask  and a little red riding hood who gives  an ashen spirit  keep going up and you'll find a grace in  a tunnel that sets you up for your first  boss fight feel free to turn around and  farm the enemies in the zone behind once  you've gotten around 1500 extra souls  you can upgrade your sword to plus two  and it will be hitting decently hard  especially with the art of war left  trigger slash at this point you can go  fight the first real boss spoiler alert  on the name margaret the fel omen you'll  probably die a good bit but you'll do  decent damage and molina will visit  again to tell you you're actually based  and take you to visit the round table  hold a key sanctuary and where you can  find a merchant selling the ashen spirit  bell in the left wing there's also a  blacksmith here too though if you want  some more wiggle room to die less in the  boss fight there are some flash upgrades  we can get head back to the agile lake  south grace and ride further south  there's another grace past the bridge  and then we're going to want to follow  the road west until we get to the  northwest tip of the peninsula head into  the church of pilgrimage and find a  sacred tier which will increase the  amount you're healed by your flask and  then keep heading south along the  coastline till you come to the fourth  church of america and find another  sacred tier  lastly we want the flask of wondrous  physics which you might have picked up  if you explored north of the wolf boy if  not head back to the north east grace  miss wood outskirts and ride up the road  until you reach the third church of  america here is another sacred tier and  a new flask that of wondrous physic this  is a new consumable that will recharge  at graces you get one sip and you can  mix different effects at graces  depending on which crystal tears you  have which is a key item crystal tears  are what we found at the minor herb tree  earlier and more can be found around  analogous trees throughout the game  though they might be a little bit harder  to acquire if you haven't upgrade your  crimson flask at the grace both charges  and healing potential in addition to  mixing your flask of wondrous physics  which you should throw in an equipment  slot  now you have a strong weapon which will  scale well into the mid and late game  with more upgrades along with some buff  flasks and maybe even an ashen spirit or  two you are well equipped and on decent  footing for the market fight you can of  course level up your characters more but  this footage of me beating market is a  samurai class that has only been leveled  up twice both going into deck's points  the weapon art slash is very strong not  only are you equipped for margat in our  journey here which is pretty easily done  within an hour of gameplay we've come  across a number of eldon rings important  mechanics weapon upgrades ever jails npc  quest lines and summoning flask upgrades  minor herd trees and map expansions to  name just a few there are plenty more  mechanics in elton ring and you'll come  across many but not all of them in your  first playthrough but now you are  prepared to a good degree you do decent  damage and can have a bit of flexibility  in assigning your future skill points  and you have an understanding of some of  the more vital game mechanics like  flasks and weapon upgrading now all  that's left to do is go explore die and  be merry in the lands between  for a final extra tidbit of loot for  those of you still watching it's  unnecessary but it's pretty strong you  can find an urge tree on the southern  peninsula it's going to be to the east  of the fourth church of america at this  earth tree you're going to find an erd  tree avatar which is a boss that you're  going to have to fight these avatars are  found at many of the minor herb trees  around the world of the lands between  but this avatar isn't too strong and  it's a good way to learn some of the  horseback mechanics and combat if you  defeat it you'll be rewarded with  another crystal tier this one negates  some degree of physical damage by giving  you a bubble shield it basically gives  you a free hit where you won't take much  damage  and that's all i have for a beginner's  guide to the early game of eldon ring  hope you'd enjoy the video and if you  want to see more elden ring content both  in guides and lore be sure to stick  around my channel  [Music]  you
 

